cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AMINE, please cite the article below."
title: "AMINE — Active Module Identification through Network Embedding"
abstract: >-
  AMINE identifies active modules in biological interaction networks by
  combining network embedding (node2vec) with a greedy module search and a
  statistical background correction. This repository is the unified,
  modernized version of the software, including a command-line interface and
  a web application.
